<title>FRANCE: Elf hopes for Azerbaijan deal in January.</title>
<headline>Elf hopes for Azerbaijan deal in January.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Elf Aquitaine is negotiating an exploration contract for the Lenkoran field in the Caspian Sea and hopes to sign a deal when Azeri president Haidar Aleiv is in Paris on January 13, a company spokesman said.</p>
<p>Foreign Affairs minister Herve de Charette said in October when he travelled the area -- which he called a new oil Eldorado -- that he had obtained &quot;very precise&quot; engagements about the role Elf could play on the Azeri oil fields.</p>
<p>Total SA, meanwhile, said it is studying &quot;the opportunity of signing an exploration contract&quot; for the same field.</p>
<p>A consortium led by Amoco will develop the fields Dan Ulduzu and Ashrafi.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
